Data. This repository does not redistribute raw datasets, with one small exception.
  scikit-learn Digits: the UCI optical recognition of handwritten digits set,
    bundled with scikit-learn. A small subset is committed as wire-level validation
    evidence under reports/results/privacy/v0150/wire/live/data/ (per seed, 8 training
    and 1 validation record for each of 4 institutions and 16 evaluator test records,
    each 8 by 8 pixels). Other saved evidence holds arrays derived from the data (captured
    model updates under wire/live/runs/, LiRA score files under v014/lira/). They are
    evidence, not copies of a dataset. No raw MNIST or Fashion-MNIST file is in Git.
  MNIST: Y. LeCun, C. Cortes and C. J. C. Burges. The originators publish no
    formal licence text and secondary sources disagree, so redistribution terms
    are treated as unverified. Users must obtain the files themselves. The
    expected SHA-256 values are pinned in src/feddisclosure/training/datasets.py
    and listed in docs/data-provenance.md.
  Fashion-MNIST: H. Xiao, K. Rasul and R. Vollgraf, Zalando Research. MIT licence, checked
    against the dataset repository on 2026-11-23. It is loaded at run time from the canonical
    host, checked against pinned SHA-256 values in
    src/feddisclosure/training/fashion_mnist.py, and is not redistributed here.
